# Implement — etude-n9b.1 workflow and manifest contract

ANCESTOR: etude-n9b (P1) — deliver GitHub issue #16 as an opt-in checkout-read
verification capability while preserving output-only as the default.

BLAST RADIUS: none outside this worktree. The implementation changes four Go
schema/codec files and creates no external state.

## Result

- Added `GateConfig.ReadCheckout` and the `read_checkout` workflow YAML leaf.
- Added `GateAttempt.ReadCheckout` and the `read_checkout` manifest JSON leaf.
- Both wire fields use `omitempty`; absent and false remain output-only and
  preserve legacy serialized output.
- Both decode paths remain strict. Tests reject near-miss field names and
  non-boolean values.
- The manifest codec test directly constructs the grant because runtime
  population belongs to dependent bead etude-n9b.2.

## Completeness audit

Repository-wide search found no non-Go schema or validator that independently
enumerates gate keys. The representation sites are the workflow domain/YAML
pair and manifest domain/JSON pair changed here. User-facing documentation is
deferred to etude-n9b.2, where the runtime behavior becomes shipped.

